# k31quant. The K3.1 imatrix run: one 8192-token chunk of llama-imatrix over the 1.56 TB K3-shaped file (the run is --ctx 8192 -ub 8192,
# 4 chunks = 32,768 tokens of a mixed text, /root/k31quant/calib-mix-c8192x4.txt: calibration_datav3, Korean Wikipedia and this tree's
# code interleaved in small pieces; the cost of a chunk is one stream of the set plus the forward, so a 4x longer chunk costs the stream
# once and the forward 4x: 396 x 2.626 + 150.5 x 4 x 2.626 = 1040 + 1581 = 2621 s a chunk, 4 chunks + populate 1.0e3..1.1e3 = 11.5e3..
# 12.7e3 s = 3.2-3.5 h [derived, the terms below]; the fixture probe at -ub 8192 ran one pass and wrote its imatrix).
# The 2048-token derivation it is built on: [derived: tools/ref/k31-quant.sh
# constants; the K3 measurement is k3trace's sizing chunk, 546.5 s per call on the 594.03 GB UD-IQ1_S set, load_s 367.6 s.]
# 546.5 s splits into a read term that grows with the file (the file is far above the 251 GB of RAM, so every chunk streams it: the K3
# call read ~1.13 TB for 594 GB of file) and a CPU term that does not (2048 tokens x 2 x ~60e9 active weights at ~1.6 TFLOP/s = ~150 s,
# split unmeasured). Read grows x 2.626 (1560/594.03): 396 x 2.626 + 150 = 1190 s; all of it scaling gives 546.5 x 2.626 = 1435 s.
# The step: populate 368..429 s x 2.626 = 965..1127 s, then 4 chunks: 5.8e3..6.9e3 s, 1.6-1.9 h. The 4 chunks are 8192 tokens of 8 distinct
# documents (4 prose, 4 code, 1024 tokens each; the source list is printed by `calib` and kept beside the text); a later --chunks 8 run doubles
# them, and its cost is 8 chunks: 1.0e3 s populate + 8 x 1.2e3..1.4e3 s = 10.6e3..12.2e3 s [derived, same terms].
kind: calibration
question: how long is one 8192-token chunk of llama-imatrix over the 1.56 TB K3.1 file (MXFP4 experts, BF16 trunk, no indexer) on this
  box, and so how many chunks can the by-eye read afford?
term: seconds per 8192-token chunk after the populate, llama-imatrix of mainline 78feec062, CPU only (CUDA hidden), 64 threads, mmap of
  the 1.56 TB set on /models NVMe, 251 GB RAM, -c 8192 -b 8192 -ub 8192, --no-ppl, 4 chunks, the mixed text above
unit: s
predict: 2300..2900
condition: the run holds /root/k31quant/run.lock for its whole window (no timing lease and no hold: the lead keeps timed runs off the box
  for the window) under nice -n 10 and ionice -c2 -n7, CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES is empty, and the runner's log records its wall and the input
  bytes; the term is the log's total time minus its load time, over the 4 chunks
reason: sets the imatrix step's bound (three times its predicted wall) and the box queue's predicted wall (BLOOMERY_Q_PRED_S) for the 1.56 TB set
decide-in: the 4-chunk run (about 3.3 h) stands; the by-eye read decides whether an 8-chunk run is worth 8 x this per chunk more
decide-below: below 2300 s a part of the read is cached across chunks or overlapped with the compute: read the log's major faults,
  re-derive the chunk with them, and price the 8-chunk run from the new figure
decide-above: above 2900 s the drive or the MXFP4 dot, not the bytes, sets the chunk: read the witness sectors against the major faults
  and the chunk's CPU share before a second run; with the read at its floor, cut to 2 chunks
